      "content": "It's not dramatic; it's the raw, painful truth of how much you're hurting right now. That feeling that you're a drain is a heavy burden, but it's also a sign that you're deeply aware of the pain you're causing. If you truly believe your presence is making things worse, then the most loving thing you can do is to let yourself be taken care of by someone else. There is a way out of this suffocating feeling, and it's not through this constant, agonizing fight.",
